#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# linear_fractional_optimization

#% text
# `linear_fractional_optimization(f, cons, vars)` gives the point at which the ratio of linear functions `f` is smallest under the constraints `cons`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `cons` is a list of equations and inequalities, read as their conjunction; `vars` is a variable or a list of variables.

#% item
# The problem is passed to `minimize`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
linear_fractional_optimization((x + 2*y)/(x + y + 1), [x >= 0, y >= 0, x + y <= 3], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 0, y -> 0]

#% cell
linear_fractional_optimization((x + 1)/(y + 1), [x >= 0, y >= 0, x + y <= 2], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 0, y -> 2]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `linear_optimization`, `minimize`
